      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "test(agents): register session lock helpers in vitest workers",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nVitest worker environments do not consistently set `process.env.VITEST` while `session-write-lock.ts` is evaluated. The test-only helper registration can therefore be skipped, causing unrelated node compact shards to fail on an undefined `sessionWriteLockTestApi`.\n\nThe production path is unchanged. The existing test-only guard additionally recognizes the Vitest worker markers used by this repository: `VITEST_MODE`, `VITEST_POOL_ID`, and `VITEST_WORKER_ID`.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact rebased head: `e2672a25b6a99748f9c76f1782b1c3bea0d2589a`\n\n- `oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/agents/session-write-lock.ts` passed.\n- `oxlint src/agents/session-write-lock.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-startup.test.ts src/gateway/server-startup-session-migration.test.ts` passed: 2 files / 17 tests.\n- `VITEST_POOL_ID=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-startup.test.ts src/gateway/server-startup-session-migration.test.ts` passed: 2 files / 17 tests.\n\nObserved target failure: `src/agents/session-write-lock.test-support.ts:44:36 TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'testing')` in node compact shards.\n",
        "branch": "fix/session-write-lock-vitest-worker-api",
